    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1173bc05-3761-5295-aa57-13939461e429",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{- 9 x}{12 x - 10}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=- 9 x$ and $v(x)=12 x - 10,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u^{\\prime}(x)&=-9,\\\\v^{\\prime}(x)&=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot (12 x - 10)-(- 9 x)\\cdot (12)}{(12 x - 10)^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{90}{\\left(12 x - 10\\right)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\frac{45}{2}}{\\left(6 x - 5\\right)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
