      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{-3}{x^{2}}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=-3$ and $v(x)=x^{2},$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u^{\\prime}(x)&=0,\\\\v^{\\prime}(x)&=2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{(0)\\cdot (x^{2})-(-3)\\cdot (2 x)}{(x^{2})^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{6 x}{\\left(x^{2}\\right)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{6}{x^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
